# Concrete types

Do not inject a concrete type. Do not register a concrete type in DI. Ever.

A constructor dependency is an interface. A DI registration is an interface to an implementation: `AddSingleton<IFoo, Foo>()`.

A concrete type appears at `new`, and only there. Tests substitute the interface.

Forbidden:

- `AddSingleton<Foo>()` or `AddScoped<Foo>()` with no interface
- A constructor parameter whose type is a class
- A test that passes `new Foo(...)` into a constructor that should take an interface
